Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:27:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 038/155] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on the identity
 remap: re-encrypt moved connections, keep the approved checkpoint

Connection secrets are encrypted under the owner's id, so a connection moved
to the new id decrypted to nothing and asked for a reconnect; the remap now
re-encrypts it with the deployment's cipher, and counts a row it cannot read
under connections_reconnect. On a forced merge the daily cost's approved
checkpoint takes the higher value instead of the sum. A test pins the copied
turn-actor label name to the server's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 omnigent/server/identity_migration_extra.py   | 40 ++++++++-
 tests/server/test_identity_migration_extra.py | 83 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 118 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/omnigent/server/identity_migration_extra.py b/omnigent/server/identity_migration_extra.py
index c693a37dcbe12125ebc808bad23d305eb23f5c35..ea1788aeb840141f73af8c589afef915c617e733 100644
--- a/omnigent/server/identity_migration_extra.py
